  <diagram id="doc-101" name="3-Questions-Assumptions">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" page="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1654" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="h101" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" value="Saeid Elkhouly — Group-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="0" width="400" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t101-0" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" value="1. Questions" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="40" width="900" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="b101-0" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=fill;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" value="&lt;table style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:12px;background:#dae8fc;color:#1A1A1A&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:40px&quot;&gt;#&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:160px&quot;&gt;SRS section&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:1000px&quot;&gt;Question&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Is the regional director a separate role? Can they temporarily run several branches, and how is the temporary period recorded?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Are opening/closing hours the same every day or different per weekday? How is a 24-hour branch shown?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;What is the pass mark for a course? Must every employee enrol in mandatory courses, and by when?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.3 / §8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Does the COO&amp;#x27;s &amp;quot;own price&amp;quot; apply to a car model or to one individual vehicle, and does it need price history?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.4, §7.13, §8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Finance wants the price charged on any day for extras and insurance. Is the price stored per rental enough, or is a price history table needed?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;6&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.6&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Must the Fleet Manager who arranged a transfer be recorded, or only the driver?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Can a blacklisting be lifted, and can a customer be blacklisted more than once?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Is a corporate contract an entity (number, dates, negotiator) or just the list of discounts?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;9&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.10&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;How many points does a rental earn? Do points expire? Can a redemption exceed the balance?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;10&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.12&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Does a rental agreement have its own number/format? What is the key?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;11&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.12&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Who are the &amp;quot;additional drivers&amp;quot;? Individual customers, authorized drivers, or anyone? What data is kept about them?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;12&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.12&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;How is the late fee calculated, and is it stored as an amount on the rental?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;13&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.16&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;What data does an invoice carry (number, month, total)? Do corporate payments settle an invoice instead of a rental?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;14&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.16&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Is a payment for a traffic fine linked to the specific violation?&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="74" width="1220" height="568" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t101-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" value="2. Assumptions" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="682" width="900" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="b101-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=fill;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" value="&lt;table style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:12px;background:#dae8fc;color:#1A1A1A&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:40px&quot;&gt;#&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:160px&quot;&gt;SRS section&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:1000px&quot;&gt;Assumption&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.12&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Rental key is RentalNumber (SRS gives none).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.15&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Supplier key is a surrogate SupplierID (SRS gives none).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.16&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Invoice entity added: InvoiceNumber, BillingMonth, IssueDate; total is derived. A payment belongs to a rental or an invoice.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;CarModel key is (Manufacturer, ModelName, ModelYear); ModelRate is per car model, with validity dates.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Branch stores Is24Hours plus opening/closing times (times empty for 24-hour branches).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;6&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;The regional director is an ordinary employee; no separate entity.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Enrollment is a weak entity identified by Employee + Course + AttemptNumber; IsMandatory is a Course attribute.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;A vehicle&amp;#x27;s current branch is optional (it may be in transit or rented).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;9&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Customer has a CustomerType (Individual/Corporate); an individual has exactly one of NationalID or PassportNumber.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;10&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Driving licence details are attributes of the individual customer; each authorized driver may match at most one individual customer (Rana&amp;#x27;s note).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;11&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;A customer is blacklisted at most once; reason, date and manager are stored on the customer.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;12&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;No separate Contract entity; only Contract_Discount (company, category, start date, percentage, end date).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;13&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.10&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Points balance and tier are derived from Loyalty_Transaction and not stored.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;14&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.12&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Additional drivers are a weak entity of the rental with only DailyFee (identity not given).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;15&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.12&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;LateFee is stored as an amount on the rental; main driver is a composite FK to the authorized driver.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;16&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.14&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Every traffic violation must be matched to exactly one rental; photo links are a multivalued attribute (own table).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;17&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.15&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Job card TotalCost is stored (default 0); parts and hours are in their own tables.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;18&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.9&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Promo discount percentage is limited to 0-100 (SRS gives no limit).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="716" width="1220" height="720" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t101-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" value="3. Contradictions" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="1476" width="900" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="b101-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=fill;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" value="&lt;table style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:12px;background:#dae8fc;color:#1A1A1A&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:40px&quot;&gt;#&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:220px&quot;&gt;SRS sections&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:940px&quot;&gt;What they say&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.1 vs §7.1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;&amp;quot;A branch is never left without a manager&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;a manager runs only one branch&amp;quot;, but the regional director temporarily takes over: if the director already runs a branch, one person runs two.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.3 vs COO note&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Pricing is &amp;quot;set per category&amp;quot;, but the COO says some luxury cars have their own price.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.7 vs §8 (Rana Adel)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Authorized drivers are &amp;quot;known only through their company&amp;quot;, but some are also individual customers.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.11 vs §12 Glossary&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Glossary defines No-Show as a *confirmed* reservation; §7.11 lists No-Show as a status without saying it must follow Confirmed.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.4/§7.13 vs §8 (Mai Ibrahim)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Finance wants the price charged on any day for categories, insurance and extras, but the SRS only keeps old rates for categories and the price-at-rental for extras and insurance.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;6&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.16 vs §7.16 (Finance note)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;A rental may have several payments, but corporate clients pay one monthly invoice instead of per rental.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="0" y="1510" width="1220" height="264" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="doc-102" name="4-Business-Rules">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1246" dy="672" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1654" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="h102" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" value="Saeid Elkhouly — Group-1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="28" width="400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t102" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1A1A1A;" value="Business rules that constraints cannot enforce" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="900" y="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="b102" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=fill;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" value="&lt;table style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:12px;background:#dae8fc;color:#1A1A1A&quot;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:40px&quot;&gt;#&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:90px&quot;&gt;SRS section&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:300px&quot;&gt;Business rule&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:350px&quot;&gt;Why constraints are not enough&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;background:#5D7F99;color:#1A1A1A;padding:4px;width:400px&quot;&gt;How to enforce it&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;A blacklisted customer cannot book again.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Needs a lookup of the customer&amp;#x27;s blacklist columns when a reservation/rental row is inserted.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Trigger on RESERVATION and RENTAL insert (or application check) that rejects customers with BlacklistDate not null.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;A person cannot be both a rental agent and a mechanic.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;PK/FK/UQ only work inside one table; the rule spans RENTAL_AGENT and MECHANIC.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Trigger on both tables that rejects an EmployeeID present in the other table.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;A branch manager must work at the branch they run.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Compares a value in BRANCH with EMPLOYEE.BranchCode of another row.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Trigger on BRANCH insert/update (or stored procedure for changing managers).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.12&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;A corporate rental must name a main driver from the company&amp;#x27;s own authorized drivers; individual rentals have none.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Depends on the customer type and a value in another table.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Trigger on RENTAL, or application logic when the agreement is created.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Rate periods of the same category must not overlap, so only one rate is valid on any date.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;A CHECK sees one row only; overlap needs other rows of the table.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Trigger (or exclusion constraint in PostgreSQL) on CATEGORY_RATE and MODEL_RATE.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;6&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.3 / O-3&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Every change of a vehicle&amp;#x27;s status must leave a trace (who and when).&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Constraints cannot create rows in another table.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Trigger on VEHICLE.CurrentStatus update that inserts into VEHICLE_STATUS_CHANGE, or a stored procedure used for all status changes.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.9&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;A promo code cannot be used more than MaxUses times and only inside its validity period.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Needs a count of other rows and a comparison with the reservation date.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Trigger or stored procedure on RESERVATION insert; usage count by a view.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;§7.10&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Redeemed points cannot exceed the customer&amp;#x27;s balance, and the tier must always be computed.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;The balance is a SUM over many rows; tier depends on it.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style=&quot;border:1px solid #6c8ebf;padding:4px;vertical-align:top&quot;&gt;Stored procedure for redemption; tier as a view/computed column over LOYALTY_TRANSACTION.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="444" width="1200" y="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
